From 570a40f3dd02acef2eb58e7da4c5194e44d82102 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Eduardo=20Garc=C3=ADa-M=C3=A1dico=20Portabella?=
 <woodyst@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 10:38:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] remoteproc: qcom_q6v5: only report a repeated handover
 once

On some platforms the handover interrupt fires again after the handover has
already been issued, and it does not do so once: measured at ~4 times a
second, indefinitely, on an SM7150 phone whose modem otherwise works fine
(data, calls and SMS all normal).

Logged at every occurrence, this one line drowns everything else. It filled
a 1 MiB ramoops console buffer with 10854 copies of itself, leaving no room
for anything else -- so the buffer that exists to preserve the last words of
a crashing kernel contained nothing but this message, and a hang under
investigation left no evidence at all. The buffer rewrites itself roughly
every 40 minutes at that rate.

Use dev_err_once(). The condition is still worth reporting, but repeating it
destroys more information than it provides.

Why the interrupt re-fires is not addressed here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
index 58d5b85..781efef 100644
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
@@ -165,7 +165,19 @@ static irqreturn_t q6v5_handover_interrupt(int irq, void *data)
 	struct qcom_q6v5 *q6v5 = data;
 
 	if (q6v5->handover_issued) {
-		dev_err(q6v5->dev, "Handover signaled, but it already happened\n");
+		/*
+		 * On some platforms this fires continuously - measured at
+		 * ~4 times a second, forever, on an SM7150 phone with a
+		 * perfectly working modem. Logged at every occurrence it
+		 * drowns the kernel log: it filled a 1 MiB ramoops console
+		 * buffer with 10854 copies of this one line, wiping every
+		 * trace of the crash that buffer existed to preserve.
+		 *
+		 * Say it once. The condition is worth knowing about, but
+		 * repeating it destroys more information than it provides.
+		 */
+		dev_err_once(q6v5->dev,
+			     "Handover signaled, but it already happened\n");
 		return IRQ_HANDLED;
 	}
 
